## 1. What This Project Is

A **modular, dataset-agnostic benchmarking framework** for binary classification, applied to two
real-world, high-imbalance domains:

| Sub-project | Dataset | Positive class | Imbalance | Primary metric |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Spam Detection** | Kaggle Spam Mails (5,172 emails) | Spam | ~29% spam | F1 / PR-AUC |
| **Fraud Detection** | Kaggle Credit Card Fraud (284,807 txns) | Fraud | 0.172% fraud | **AUPRC** |

It trains, evaluates, visualizes, and reports on **multiple classifiers in scaled and unscaled
regimes**, tracks every run with **MLflow**, and emits **publication-ready figures and PDF/Excel
reports** per dataset.

---

## 2. Why It Matters

Binary classifiers behave very differently under class imbalance and feature scaling. This framework
makes the trade-offs **measurable, visual, and reproducible**:

- **Spam**: false positives (legitimate mail blocked) vs. false negatives (spam delivered)
- **Fraud**: false positives (declined customers) vs. false negatives (missed fraud — costly)

Both are framed against **anomaly detection**, since rare-positive problems are fundamentally
anomaly problems (see the two domain reports).

---

## 3. How It Works

```
KaggleDataLoader ──▶ ClassifierGroupComparer ──▶ ModelVisualizer ──▶ reports/
                          │                                            ├── figures/*.png
                          ├── MLflow tracking (mlruns/)                └── docs/*.pdf, *.xlsx
                          └── scaled vs. unscaled model groups
```

| Module | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| `core/data_loader.py` — `KaggleDataLoader` | Download, cache, prepare Kaggle datasets |
| `core/comparer.py` — `ClassifierGroupComparer` | Split, train scaled & unscaled groups, collect metrics |
| `core/visualizer.py` — `ModelVisualizer` | Confusion matrices, F1 bars, group comparison, ROC & PR curves, Excel/PDF |
| `core/utils.py` | Shared helpers (paths, seeds, error handling) |
| `main.py` | End-to-end driver per dataset + report name |
| `mlruns/` | Auto-generated MLflow experiment store |

Metrics per model: Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1, Confusion Matrix, ROC-AUC, PR-AUC.
Models that cannot run (e.g., MultinomialNB on negative inputs) are **skipped and reported**.

---

## 4. Results at a Glance (with visuals)

### 4.1 Spam Detection (moderate imbalance)

- **Best scaled:** LogisticRegression, MLPClassifier
- **Best unscaled:** LightGBM, XGBoost
- **Trade-offs:** SVC → cautious (high precision, low recall) · KNN → aggressive (high recall, low precision)

