Full report → [`spam_fraud_detector/reports/spam_detection/docs/SPAM_DETECTION.md`](spam_fraud_detector/reports/spam_detection/docs/SPAM_DETECTION.md)

### 4.2 Fraud Detection (severe imbalance)

- **Best scaled:** KNN, MLPClassifier
- **Best unscaled:** RandomForest, XGBoost
- **Trade-offs:** SVC avoids false alarms but misses fraud · GradientBoosting struggles with recall

<p align="center">
  <img src="spam_fraud_detector/reports/fraud_detection/figures/fraud_detection_f1_scores.png" alt="Fraud F1 scores" width="48%"/>
  <img src="spam_fraud_detector/reports/fraud_detection/figures/fraud_detection_precision_recall_curves.png" alt="Fraud PR curves" width="48%"/>
</p>
<p align="center">
  <img src="spam_fraud_detector/reports/fraud_detection/figures/fraud_detection_group_comparison.png" alt="Fraud group comparison" width="48%"/>
  <img src="spam_fraud_detector/reports/fraud_detection/figures/fraud_detection_confusion_matrices.png" alt="Fraud confusion matrices" width="48%"/>
</p>
<p align="center"><img src="spam_fraud_detector/reports/fraud_detection/figures/fraud_detection_roc_curves.png" alt="Fraud ROC curves" width="70%"/></p>

> ⚠️ Accuracy is misleading on fraud data (a constant "legitimate" predictor scores **99.828%**).
> Use **AUPRC + recall at fixed precision** and the confusion matrix.
> Full report → [`spam_fraud_detector/reports/fraud_detection/docs/FRAUD_DETECTION.md`](spam_fraud_detector/reports/fraud_detection/docs/FRAUD_DETECTION.md)

